# Canonical acceptance inputs are tracked for clean-checkout validation. New runs
# use agent-engineering-acceptance/runs/<runId>/ (ignored); only promote accepted
# final results into runtime-authority-convergence-final/ after validation.
# Never run plan/full with the tracked canonical directory as the output target.
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/
artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/*
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/
artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/*
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/changed-path-ownership.json
# The canonical accepted engineering evidence pair. The control pack
# (tests/unit/runtime-authority-convergence-control-pack.test.ts) requires STATUS.md
# to point at these paths *and* loads them, so they must exist in a fresh checkout.
# `full` writes runs/<runId>/ and the canonical copy is promoted into this directory
# afterwards, so tracking them never dirties a running acceptance.
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/manifest.json
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/final-report.json
!artifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/human-verdict.yaml
